Hint:\(m=\frac{v}{u}\)

Step: Find the focal length of the lens.
The magnification of the lens is given by;
\(\Rightarrow ​​​​​​​ m=\frac{f}{u+f} \)
When an object is placed at \(10~\text{cm}\), then the magnification is given
by;
\(\Rightarrow +m=\frac{f}{-10+f} ~~~...(1)\)
When an object is placed at \(20~\text{cm}\), then the magnification is given
by;
\(\Rightarrow -m=\frac{f}{-20+f}~~~...(2)\)
From equations (1) and (2), we get;
\(\Rightarrow -1=\frac{f-20}{f-10} \)
The focal length of the lens is given by;
\(\Rightarrow 30=2 f \Rightarrow f=15 ~\text{cm}\)
